significant":false,"nucleus_direction":"lower in AD","nucleus_padj":0.295946,"nucleus_log2fc":-0.0178411,"nucleus_score":-1.20445,"pct_ad":0.136631,"pct_control":0.143404,"donor_test":"not significant","donor_padj":0.99429,"donor_log2fc":-0.017528,"donor_lfcse":0.0805552,"donor_log2fc_shrunk":-6.84871e-05},{"cell_type":"In","gene_symbol":"TCEB3","gene_symbol_current":"ELOA","gene_id":"ENSG00000011007","nucleus_tested":false,"nucleus_significant":null,"nucleus_direction":"not tested","nucleus_padj":null,"nucleus_log2fc":null,"nucleus_score":null,"pct_ad":null,"pct_control":null,"donor_test":"not significant","donor_padj":0.999889,"donor_log2fc":0.0252666,"donor_lfcse":0.150101,"donor_log2fc_shrunk":1.16941e-06}],"modules":[],"degas_bulk_de":false,"drug_target":false}},"description":[{"gene_id":"ENSG00000011007","entrez_id":["6924"],"uniprot":["Q14241"],"ncbi_summary":"This gene encodes the protein elongin A, which is a subunit of the transcription factor B (SIII) complex. The SIII complex is composed of elongins A/A2, B and C. It activates elongation by RNA polymerase II by suppressing transient pausing of the polymerase at many sites within transcription units. Elongin A functions as the transcriptionally active component of the SIII complex, whereas elongins B and C are regulatory subunits. Elongin A2 is specifically expressed in the testis, and capable of forming a stable complex with elongins B and C. The von Hippel-Lindau tumor suppressor protein binds to elongins B and C, and thereby inhibits transcription elongation. [provided by RefSeq, Jul 2008].","ncbi_source":"NCBI Gene summary (RefSeq), via MyGene.info","uniprot_function":[{"accession":"Q14241","text":"SIII, also known as elongin, is a general transcription elongation factor that increases the RNA polymerase II transcription elongation past template-encoded arresting sites. Subunit A is transcriptionally active and its transcription activity is strongly enhanced by binding to the dimeric complex of the SIII regulatory subunits B and C (elongin BC complex). As part of a multisubunit complex composed of elongin BC complex (ELOB and ELOC), elongin A/ELOA, RBX1 and CUL5; polyubiquitinates monoubiquitinated POLR2A."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_03","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}